3691
03:08:54,500 --> 03:08:55,380
Maybe, like...

3692
03:08:55,380 --> 03:08:56,760
Below ten years or something?

3693
03:08:56,900 --> 03:08:57,740
Maybe around ten years?

3694
03:08:58,600 --> 03:09:00,120
Was that scary as a kid?

3695
03:09:00,580 --> 03:09:03,480
Because I can imagine being terrified of that as a kid.

3696
03:09:05,340 --> 03:09:06,580
As an adult, it's...

3697
03:09:06,580 --> 03:09:07,480
It's, you know, it's okay.

3698
03:09:07,740 --> 03:09:08,640
It's not too bad.

3699
03:09:09,480 --> 03:09:10,860
But as a kid...

3700
03:09:10,860 --> 03:09:11,580
Oh...

3701
03:09:12,880 --> 03:09:15,280
I mean, as a kid, I was super scared of The Mummy.

3702
03:09:15,620 --> 03:09:17,060
You know, the Brendan Fraser movie?

3703
03:09:18,620 --> 03:09:20,240
Nowadays, I kind of laugh at it.

3704
03:09:20,480 --> 03:09:21,740
It's not that scary anymore.

3705
03:09:24,910 --> 03:09:26,810
Absolutely, but not as scary as the...

3706
03:09:26,810 --> 03:09:27,750
Red...

3707
03:09:27,750 --> 03:09:28,470
Redettes?

3708
03:09:28,810 --> 03:09:31,350
Oh, are you talking about the ones that go...

3709
03:09:32,070 --> 03:09:33,010
And freeze you?

3710
03:09:33,050 --> 03:09:34,090
Because those are creepy.

3711
03:09:35,110 --> 03:09:36,230
I agree with that.

3712
03:09:39,720 --> 03:09:43,900
I think those ceiling hands were the inspiration for the teleporter hands inside the stranger.

3713
03:09:45,600 --> 03:09:47,880
The teleporter hands inside the stranger.

3714
03:09:49,960 --> 03:09:52,400
Are you talking about...

3715
03:09:53,460 --> 03:09:54,840
Out of Wilds?

3716
03:09:56,000 --> 03:10:01,060
I thought you were about to say Elden Ring, those hands that were moving around and grabbing you.

3717
03:10:01,780 --> 03:10:03,140
Because that's what I thought.

3718
03:10:04,880 --> 03:10:06,940
Now I think those were inspired by Zelda.

3719
03:10:10,440 --> 03:10:11,280
I see, okay.

3720
03:10:12,000 --> 03:10:12,640
Yeah, maybe.

3721
03:10:17,080 --> 03:10:20,700
There were hands in the original NES game, so I was kind of used to it.

3722
03:10:22,280 --> 03:10:22,680
Okay.

3723
03:10:23,080 --> 03:10:24,420
It was a common enemy to have hands.

3724
03:10:28,180 --> 03:10:31,600
How did you like losing the race twice to a total scammer?

3725
03:10:32,720 --> 03:10:33,540
Dude, right?

3726
03:10:34,000 --> 03:10:35,980
I thought I was losing my mind at first.

3727
03:10:36,800 --> 03:10:39,920
I was pretty sure he said three minutes and thirty-something seconds.

3728
03:10:40,200 --> 03:10:42,440
And then all of a sudden I was one second faster.

3729
03:10:42,700 --> 03:10:44,240
It was almost too good to be true.

3730
03:10:45,900 --> 03:10:47,380
It didn't feel good, let me tell you.

3731
03:10:47,640 --> 03:10:48,760
And I'm gonna get back...

3732
03:10:48,760 --> 03:10:49,800
I'm gonna get it back, you know?

3733
03:10:49,880 --> 03:10:51,160
I'm gonna get my revenge one day.

3734
03:10:53,340 --> 03:10:55,860
Which reminds me, do you know how to make a plumber cry?

3735
03:10:56,580 --> 03:10:58,360
Or even the runner in this case?

3736
03:11:04,460 --> 03:11:08,340
By the time you finish this game, you'll see its influence everywhere else.

3737
03:11:10,020 --> 03:11:11,440
Um, I guess so.

3738
03:11:11,740 --> 03:11:12,640
Is this a dad joke?

3739
03:11:12,900 --> 03:11:13,600
Yeah, kinda.

3740
03:11:13,760 --> 03:11:15,160
The answer is you kill his whole family.

3741
03:11:16,120 --> 03:11:18,700
Because there's no way he's not gonna cry if you do that.

3742
03:11:19,400 --> 03:11:20,860
For sure he's gonna cry.

3743
03:11:21,980 --> 03:11:22,420
Right?

3744
03:11:22,420 --> 03:11:25,560
Like, there's no way a couple tears won't be streaming down.

3745
03:11:26,520 --> 03:11:28,040
You put me to sleep today, Oliver?

3746
03:11:28,300 --> 03:11:28,800
Ha ha ha!

3747
03:11:29,340 --> 03:11:31,220
I don't know if that's a good or bad thing.

3748
03:11:31,800 --> 03:11:32,920
I hope that's good.

3749
03:11:34,280 --> 03:11:35,560
What if he hates his family?

3750
03:11:35,820 --> 03:11:37,100
Well, I guess I failed then.

3751
03:11:37,280 --> 03:11:37,660
Then he...

3752
03:11:37,660 --> 03:11:39,360
Then he cries from happiness.

3753
03:11:41,200 --> 03:11:43,460
This game copied so much from Breath of the Wild.

3754
03:11:43,580 --> 03:11:44,060
I know!

3755
03:11:45,000 --> 03:11:47,420
Like, Gerudo and all the others sound...

3756
03:11:47,420 --> 03:11:49,520
They're exactly like the ones from Breath of the Wild.

3757
03:11:49,640 --> 03:11:50,120
How dare they?

3758
03:11:53,560 --> 03:11:54,560
Maybe he was abused.

3759
03:11:54,700 --> 03:11:55,020
Yeah, maybe.

3760
03:11:55,540 --> 03:11:57,320
I mean, for him to turn out like that?

3761
03:11:57,440 --> 03:11:58,340
I better hope so.

3762
03:12:01,100 --> 03:12:02,060
That's Danish joke.

3763
03:12:02,260 --> 03:12:04,760
It is actually kinda a joke I heard in Danish.

3764
03:12:05,060 --> 03:12:07,540
You would say Bliggenslayer in Danish.

3765
03:12:11,220 --> 03:12:12,500
Copying a game from the future?

3766
03:12:12,620 --> 03:12:13,140
I mean, listen.

3767
03:12:13,820 --> 03:12:15,220
The game has time travel, right?

3768
03:12:15,240 --> 03:12:15,980
It all makes sense.

3769
03:12:18,400 --> 03:12:20,040
How do you like the Gerudo Vala music?

3770
03:12:20,140 --> 03:12:20,840
I think it's...

3771
03:12:20,840 --> 03:12:21,980
I think it's a banger.

3772
03:12:23,280 --> 03:12:26,180
I'm bobbing my head constantly when I'm riding my horse through that part.

3773
03:12:30,920 --> 03:12:32,980
I forget which northern country has that phrase.

3774
03:12:33,080 --> 03:12:33,400
Which one?

3775
03:12:34,520 --> 03:12:37,340
Oh, speaking of family and death, do you guys have the winter greeting?

3776
03:12:37,480 --> 03:12:39,200
Have you lost any uncles this winter?

3777
03:12:39,360 --> 03:12:39,680
No.

3778
03:12:40,560 --> 03:12:41,640
We don't say that.

3779
03:12:43,140 --> 03:12:43,860
That's dark.

3780
03:12:44,240 --> 03:12:47,480
It's like, oh, we lost two uncles last winter.

3781
03:12:48,360 --> 03:12:49,540
It was a harsh one.

3782
03:12:50,880 --> 03:12:52,400
A lot of good bangers in this game.

3783
03:12:52,540 --> 03:12:53,260
Indeed, I agree.

3784
03:12:55,040 --> 03:12:56,820
The spirit song is incredible.

3785
03:12:57,440 --> 03:13:00,860
Like, it puts me in a kind of mood I can't explain.

3786
03:13:01,840 --> 03:13:04,820
In a mood where I'm just like, I feel free and I can fly.

3787
03:13:05,120 --> 03:13:06,380
And I want to know more.

3788
03:13:07,240 --> 03:13:12,120
It sounds super stupid when I say it like that, but there's something about those notes.

3789
03:13:12,240 --> 03:13:12,940
They hit just right.

3790
03:13:16,370 --> 03:13:18,250
Yeah, it's a weird phrase, but I think it's funny.

3791
03:13:20,330 --> 03:13:23,610
I lost three uncles last winter, but got a new one last summer.

3792
03:13:24,470 --> 03:13:25,350
Is that real?

3793
03:13:27,130 --> 03:13:28,690
That's crazy, if that's true.

3794
03:13:32,730 --> 03:13:34,930
Gerudo Valley music and Song of Storms are goaded.

3795
03:13:35,590 --> 03:13:38,490
For me so far, Song of Storms is number one.

3796
03:13:39,250 --> 03:13:46,150
And even though we only heard just like 10 seconds of this melody, I would say the spirit melody is second.

3797
03:13:47,210 --> 03:13:47,650
third?

3798
03:13:48,810 --> 03:13:50,430
Yeah, it's gotta be Gerudo Valley.

3799
03:13:51,390 --> 03:13:52,470
That's the third song.

3800
03:13:52,930 --> 03:13:55,470
After that, it's starting to blur a little bit in my mind.

3801
03:13:56,010 --> 03:13:56,530
Oh, no, no, no.

3802
03:13:56,830 --> 03:13:57,010
No.

3803
03:13:57,330 --> 03:14:01,150
I think I'm gonna say Lost Woods 3 and then Gerudo 4.

3804
03:14:02,850 --> 03:14:03,290
Yeah.

3805
03:14:04,370 --> 03:14:05,210
In that order.

3806
03:14:06,810 --> 03:14:07,490
So far.

3807
03:14:12,500 --> 03:14:13,440
Did I miss something?

3808
03:14:13,600 --> 03:14:16,780
You rode around and listened to Gerudo music and where did you hear the spirit song?

3809
03:14:16,860 --> 03:14:18,380
It's from the from the ocarina.

3810
03:14:19,600 --> 03:14:21,300
You know when you do the...

3811
03:14:21,300 --> 03:14:23,220
I forgot the melody now, but...

3812
03:14:23,220 --> 03:14:24,380
The last one I got.

3813
03:14:28,780 --> 03:14:30,560
If you wanna hear any of the songs, YouTube...

3814
03:14:30,560 --> 03:14:31,380
Oh, yeah, of course, of course.

3815
03:14:34,420 --> 03:14:36,900
I'm definitely gonna listen to the soundtrack when I'm done with the game.

3816
03:14:41,140 --> 03:14:42,780
Yeah, the sequel is Majora's Mask.

3817
03:14:43,280 --> 03:14:43,640
Right?

3818
03:14:45,860 --> 03:14:47,800
Wasn't the last one the serenade of water?

3819
03:14:48,580 --> 03:14:51,140
No, no, I got one today where I can go to the desert.

3820
03:14:53,080 --> 03:14:53,980
Maybe I'm wrong.

3821
03:14:54,060 --> 03:14:55,640
Maybe the term of...

3822
03:14:55,640 --> 03:14:57,000
name of it wasn't Spirit.

3823
03:14:57,160 --> 03:15:00,200
Wasn't that something Serenade of Spirit or something?

3824
03:15:00,280 --> 03:15:00,900
What was the name of it?

3825
03:15:02,620 --> 03:15:04,540
The last song I got on my ocarina.

3826
03:15:05,440 --> 03:15:06,200
Requiem of Spirit.

3827
03:15:06,360 --> 03:15:06,880
Thanks, that one.

3828
03:15:08,140 --> 03:15:08,820
Yeah, that one's good.

3829
03:15:12,170 --> 03:15:13,010
That's my second.

3830
03:15:13,750 --> 03:15:15,610
And then Lost Woods and then Gerudo.

3831
03:15:17,870 --> 03:15:18,990
Look up Zelda Wave.

3832
03:15:19,170 --> 03:15:21,830
There's a good mix of the Ocarina of Time songs.

3833
03:15:22,330 --> 03:15:23,910
Is that like a remix though?

3834
03:15:24,190 --> 03:15:25,930
Or is it just the original?

3835
03:15:26,210 --> 03:15:30,750
Because, I mean, why would it just be called Zelda Wave if it's just the original songs?

3836
03:15:33,410 --> 03:15:34,110
I don't know.

3837
03:15:34,230 --> 03:15:35,830
This magical world, it's like...

3838
03:15:38,130 --> 03:15:38,570
Okay.

3839
03:15:38,850 --> 03:15:40,430
This is gonna sound cheesy as hell.

3840
03:15:41,970 --> 03:15:48,070
But you ever get this feeling when you start Lord of the Rings, you know, it's like a long trilogy, you know?

3841
03:15:48,150 --> 03:15:51,110
There's like 10 hours if you do the extended in total.

3842
03:15:51,410 --> 03:15:59,270
And when you start that movie and you hear this music, you just know that you're gonna be transported into this world and there's this whole adventure in front of you.

3843
03:15:59,630 --> 03:16:00,070
You know?

3844
03:16:00,130 --> 03:16:03,750
And all this stuff is gonna happen and it's great and it's like a great escape from everything.

3845
03:16:04,390 --> 03:16:08,570
Just knowing that all of that is ahead and the world exists and there's all these people and all of that.

3846
03:16:09,310 --> 03:16:12,390
That's what I feel when I hear the start of that song, but like for a different world.

3847
03:16:12,730 --> 03:16:14,490
A world I don't even know what is.

3848
03:16:15,070 --> 03:16:20,330
A different world, completely different from Zelda and everything, but Maybe a little science fiction-y.

3849
03:16:20,770 --> 03:16:22,410
You know, Dune-ish.

3850
03:16:22,510 --> 03:16:22,830
I don't know.

3851
03:16:22,910 --> 03:16:24,870
Maybe not Dune, but something like it.

3852
03:16:25,050 --> 03:16:25,610
I don't know.

3853
03:16:27,030 --> 03:16:28,310
Makes me happy, man.

3854
03:16:29,610 --> 03:16:30,570
Mountains, Gandalf.

3855
03:16:30,770 --> 03:16:31,610
I want to see mountains.

3856
03:16:37,310 --> 03:16:40,810
Having played it now, now you can tell why it's stuck with so many people.

3857
03:16:40,910 --> 03:16:42,110
Yeah, I get it now.

3858
03:16:42,970 --> 03:16:45,770
I really did expect this game to be underwhelming.

3859
03:16:46,450 --> 03:16:47,350
And it isn't.

3860
03:16:48,250 --> 03:16:53,250
I thought I was going to, you know, hate on it a little bit because of the age.

3861
03:16:54,450 --> 03:16:57,890
But that doesn't even play a factor for me at all.

3862
03:17:00,710 --> 03:17:01,870
Congrats on getting Epona.

3863
03:17:02,050 --> 03:17:02,390
Thank you.

3864
03:17:02,590 --> 03:17:03,370
Thank you very much.

3865
03:17:03,510 --> 03:17:04,310
It was a hard battle.

3866
03:17:08,460 --> 03:17:09,460
We were rooting for you.

3867
03:17:09,580 --> 03:17:09,900
Thank you.

3868
03:17:09,980 --> 03:17:10,660
I appreciate it.

3869
03:17:12,220 --> 03:17:15,000
Koji Kondo wrote some of the best compositions for games.

3870
03:17:15,320 --> 03:17:16,840
He did Zelda and Mario games.

3871
03:17:16,840 --> 03:17:17,200
Ooh.

3872
03:17:18,760 --> 03:17:20,060
Is he still doing music today?

3873
03:17:22,620 --> 03:17:25,060
Because I'm kind of curious to hear what he would make today.

3874
03:17:30,380 --> 03:17:32,200
You warming up to Ocarina of Time?

3875
03:17:32,360 --> 03:17:34,300
His insane character arc progression, is it?

3876
03:17:35,000 --> 03:17:36,820
I mean, it's a very well-beloved game.

3877
03:17:37,020 --> 03:17:39,040
It's not a surprise, I guess, that I like it.

3878
03:17:40,600 --> 03:17:43,420
I guess statistically, it would be weird for me not to like it.

3879
03:17:44,000 --> 03:17:46,140
Just because of how good it is, apparently, right?

3880
03:17:49,870 --> 03:17:51,290
He still does Mario and Zelda?

3881
03:17:51,470 --> 03:17:53,810
Damn, he's been doing that same series for so long?

3882
03:17:54,410 --> 03:17:55,910
Is he not doing anything else?

3883
03:17:56,110 --> 03:17:57,290
He must get tired of that.

3884
03:18:00,410 --> 03:18:02,210
I think you'd like Final Fantasy music?

3885
03:18:02,310 --> 03:18:02,930
You think so?

3886
03:18:03,030 --> 03:18:03,890
I don't know, man.

3887
03:18:04,570 --> 03:18:06,450
That's like the whole anime stuff, right?

3888
03:18:07,010 --> 03:18:07,830
I don't know.

3889
03:18:08,310 --> 03:18:09,710
Maybe it'll be cringe for me.

3890
